(6734247, 1008305, 37629, '<td valign="top">this is almost there. I would have set up the props a little differently. the bit of shaving that is falling out of the frame is somewhat distracting and I would have pulled together all the little bits of wood chips that look like they might be dust on your sensor. I''d look up the rule of thirds as a start in aiding the composition. The exposure settings on your camera are also a bit too dark. For shots like these, if you don''t have the proper lighting inside, take it outside on a nice day, usually the best light you can get.</td>', 'this is almost there. I would have set up the props a little differently. the bit of shaving that is falling out of the frame is somewhat distracting and I would have pulled together all the little bits of wood chips that look like they might be dust on your sensor. I''d look up the rule of thirds as a start in aiding the composition. The exposure settings on your camera are also a bit too dark. For shots like these, if you don''t have the proper lighting inside, take it outside on a nice day, usually the best light you can get.', '2012-04-06 11:24:04.000000', NULL, 1),
