(6734853, 1007276, 128323, '<td valign="top">I''ve already come back to this one at least 3 or 4 times trying to figure out how you''ve done this.  My guess is that you''ve carved out a space for the glass in whatever surface you''ve used, and that surface is either water-repellant or you''ve put some kind of oil on it to make the water bead up.  In any case, it''s a brilliant way to say "liquify".  Awesome shot!  (voted earlier)</td>', 'I''ve already come back to this one at least 3 or 4 times trying to figure out how you''ve done this.  My guess is that you''ve carved out a space for the glass in whatever surface you''ve used, and that surface is either water-repellant or you''ve put some kind of oil on it to make the water bead up.  In any case, it''s a brilliant way to say "liquify".  Awesome shot!  (voted earlier)', '2012-04-07 07:04:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(6734854, 1008453, 128323, '<td valign="top">I''ve never seen an orange sky like that!  amazing shot, and apt title!</td>', 'I''ve never seen an orange sky like that!  amazing shot, and apt title!', '2012-04-07 07:05:04.000000', NULL, 1),
