(6740802, 1007276, 18563, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tanguera:</b></div><hr/><i> How do you get such perfect drops?!  Congrats on the ribbon. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks Johanna!<br/> <br/>Here was my setup: <br/> <br/>The base was cover to a plastic filing folder with a hole cut in the middle to fit the glass. Underneath the base I epoxied a plastic container so that water could be poured around the glass and overflow onto the base. I used duct tape to secure the glass to the bottom of the plastic container, filled with water and used a small syringe to add the droplets around the puddle. As far as lighting, I used 2 AlienBee B800 at 1/4 power aimed at a white reflector for the backdrop.<br/> <br/>~Chris</td>', 'Originally posted by tanguera: How do you get such perfect drops?!  Congrats on the ribbon.   Thanks Johanna! Here was my setup:  The base was cover to a plastic filing folder with a hole cut in the middle to fit the glass. Underneath the base I epoxied a plastic container so that water could be poured around the glass and overflow onto the base. I used duct tape to secure the glass to the bottom of the plastic container, filled with water and used a small syringe to add the droplets around the puddle. As far as lighting, I used 2 AlienBee B800 at 1/4 power aimed at a white reflector for the backdrop. ~Chris', '2012-04-13 14:52:10.000000', NULL, 0),
